{
	title: 'Find previews the selected row beside the results',
	spec: 'When the Find dialog is wide (web: viewport from 1200px; terminal: box interior from 160 columns), a preview pane sits right of the results. It shows the selected row card among its neighbors in history order (3 before, 3 after), each labeled with its card id and why label, every query match marked and the hit card lit like a selected row, scrolled so the hit sits about a third down. A tab row previews its best-evidence card the same way; a tab row without card evidence (title or cwd match, recent tabs) previews its last cards. Neighbors show at most 6 lines or 400 characters; the hit card at most 30 lines or 1600 characters starting a few lines above its first match. The previous preview stays until the next arrives: the pane never blanks between selections. Narrow dialogs show no pane. The worker reads previews from the find index: the find-preview command answers with a find-preview event; a failure shows in the pane.',
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'Previews read neighbors by docs rowid within the session (history insertion order); about 3-5 ms on the real index, so no extra SQLite index or version bump. The web dialog wraps the list and pane in .body, display: contents for other modals.'
	],
